---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const principles = [
  {
    name: 'Useful first',
    line: 'Every guide opens with why it matters to real work and ends with an exercise you can run tonight.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Checkable objectives',
    line: 'The objective box promises observable verbs (estimate, restructure, diagnose), never "understand"; you can check whether you got them.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Active recall',
    line: 'The self-check at the end of each guide makes you pull the ideas back out of your own head: reveal-style answers, no grades.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Prerequisites are explicit',
    line: 'Prerequisite links and the Broad → Practitioner → Deep levels mean each guide builds on ones you have read instead of assuming them.',
  },
];
---

<Base title="How it’s built · CoreWise Academy">
  <main>
    <p class="mono-label accent">How it’s built</p>
    <h1 class="display">How guides get made</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2><span class="no">01</span>Every guide starts with a video the editor learned from</h2>
      <p>
        The transcript is fetched and broken into concepts, prerequisites, misconceptions,
        exercises, and quotable moments with timestamps. A source registry records every ingested
        video and why it qualified.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="no">02</span>Several sources become one original guide</h2>
      <p>
        Notes from multiple sources are combined into an original guide; the site never republishes
        anyone's lecture. The writing tool reads the whole curriculum first and decides whether the
        material becomes a new guide, extends an existing one, or splits across several.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="no">03</span>An editor reviews every guide before it publishes</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing publishes directly. Every draft arrives as a pull request; the editor reviews,
        corrects, and merges. Merging is publishing: the site rebuilds and the guide goes live.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="no">04</span>Learning science, applied</h2>
      <ul class="principles">
        {
          principles.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{p.name}.</strong> {p.line}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="no">05</span>Built like it teaches</h2>
      <p>
        The site itself is a static Astro build: design tokens in one documented file, a custom
        titling typeface generated from stroke skeletons, and a WebGL star chart whose stars are
        the guides themselves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    main { max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--s-4)); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s-8) var(--s-4) var(--s-12); }
    h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, var(--text-3xl)); margin: var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-4); }
    .prose p { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
    .prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 400; margin: var(--s-6) 0 var(--s-2); }
    .no { color: var(--accent-deep); margin-right: 0.45em; }
    .principles { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .principles li { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-deep); padding-left: var(--s-3); margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
  </style>
</Base>
